@ 6.2.2.1.14 - Classical Arabic to Moroccan Arabic
# citation: Pogostick Man, from http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moroccan_Arabic
	t > t͜s / plain t only, distinguishable from the sequence t͡s
	{a,i} > ə / ; the change of short a blocked for some speakers before ħ ʕ
	u > ə
	C:[+labial/+velar] > ʷ / adjacent to short u
	{u,ə} > ∅ // C_C{ C#, # }
	ə > a
	ə > ɐ
	ə > ɪ
	u > ʊ
	{ a:[+long], i:[+long], u:[+long] } > { ɑ:[+long], e:[+long], o:[+long] }
	a:[+long] > æ:[+long]
	C:[+phargyn]C > CCˤ
	C:[+phargyn] > C / :{ #_V, V_V }:
	q > q, ɡ
	d͡ʒ > d, ɡ / if s or z occur somewhere in the word
	d͡ʒ > ʒ
	s > ʃ / if ʃ is somewhere in the stem after it
	z > ʒ / if ʒ is somewhere in the stem after it